{"name":"Costa Del Sol","hex":"#625d2a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"costa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of rib.","A riblike part of a plant or animal, such as a midrib of a leaf or a thickened vein or the margin of an insect wing.\n The vein forming the leading edge of most insect wings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/costa"},{"term":"del","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Delaware languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The symbol ∇ used to denote the gradient operator.","the symbol ∂, in the context of a partial differential"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/del"},{"term":"sol","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Solos."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In a movable-do or tonic sol-fa system: the fifth step in a scale, preceded by fa and followed by la.\n\nIn a fixed-do system: the musical note G.","In a movable-do or tonic sol-fa system: the fifth step in a scale, preceded by fa and followed by la."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sol"}],"entries":[{"title":"Costa del Sol","blocks":[{"text":"The Costa del Sol is a region in the south of Spain in the autonomous community of Andalusia, comprising the coastal towns and communities along the coastline of the Province of Málaga and the eastern part of Campo de Gibraltar in Cádiz. Formerly made up only of a series of small fishing settlements, today the region is a world-renowned tourist destination. The Costa del Sol is situated between two lesser known coastal regions, the Costa de la Luz and the Costa Tropical."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Litoral_entre_Marbella_y_Fuengirola_-_50003391192.jpg/330px-Litoral_entre_Marbella_y_Fuengirola_-_50003391192.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costa_del_Sol"},{"title":"Del","blocks":[{"text":"Del, or nabla, is an operator used in mathematics as a vector differential operator, usually represented by ∇. When applied to a function defined on a one-dimensional domain, it denotes the standard derivative of the function as defined in calculus. When applied to a field, it may denote any one of three operations depending on the way it is applied: the gradient or (locally) steepest slope of a scalar field ; the divergence of a vector field; or the curl (rotation) of a vector field."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Del"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Puerto_Ban%C3%BAs_Marbella.jpg/500px-Puerto_Ban%C3%BAs_Marbella.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Puerto_Ban%C3%BAs_Marbella.jpg/1280px-Puerto_Ban%C3%BAs_Marbella.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Puerto_Ban%C3%BAs_Marbella.jpg/500px-Puerto_Ban%C3%BAs_Marbella.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuerto_Ban%C3%BAs_Marbella.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Balconyofeurope_nerja.jpg/500px-Balconyofeurope_nerja.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Balconyofeurope_nerja.jpg/1280px-Balconyofeurope_nerja.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Balconyofeurope_nerja.jpg/500px-Balconyofeurope_nerja.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABalconyofeurope_nerja.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo